<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices remain firm on good demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices remain firm on good demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices continued firm on Thursday in central Indian markets on limited arrivals and good demand from processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices rose by 100-150 rupees per tonne on higher business volume and strong undertone.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were almost at previous levels in thin trade. Soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees per tonne on limited demand in local market.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were firm on gaining overseas markets.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was quoted at $278-279 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $127-128 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,350 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,300-4,325 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
